  "details": "<p><span>This tomb was excavated from 1875 to 1877. It was located on the north side of the via Praenestina, ca. 100 m. inside the Porta Maggiore at the south-west side of the modern Viale Principessa Margherita. The tomb's three chambers included a wealth of inscriptions dating\u00a0<span>from Augustus to Claudius.</span></span></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A columbarium tomb of the slaves and freedmen of the Statilii, and of M. Statilius Taurus, consul in A.D. 44.",
